This is a miscompilation bug in InstCombine.
Issue title: [clang] Miscompile with -O3 and -O0/1/2 since 18.1.0
Detailed information:
Source:
target datalayout = "e-p:64:64:64-i1:8:8-i8:8:8-i16:16:16-i32:32:32-i64:64:64-f32:32:32-f64:64:64-v64:64:64-v128:128:128-a0:0:64-s0:64:64-f80:128:128-n8:16:32:64"

define i64 @wrong_gep_arg_into_phi(ptr noundef %ptr) {
entry:
  ret i64 0
}

Target:
target datalayout = "e-p:64:64:64-i1:8:8-i8:8:8-i16:16:16-i32:32:32-i64:64:64-f32:32:32-f64:64:64-v64:64:64-v128:128:128-a0:0:64-s0:64:64-f80:128:128-n8:16:32:64"

define i64 @wrong_gep_arg_into_phi(ptr %ptr) {
entry:
  %val = load i8, ptr null, align 1
  ret i64 0
}

Transformation doesn't verify!

ERROR: Source is more defined than target

Example:
ptr noundef %ptr = pointer(non-local, block_id=0, offset=3) / Address=#x3

Source:

SOURCE MEMORY STATE
===================
NON-LOCAL BLOCKS:
Block 0 >	size: 0	align: 1	alloc type: 0	alive: false	address: 0
Block 1 >	size: 0	align: 1	alloc type: 0	alive: true	address: 1

Target:
i8 %val = UB triggered!


Summary:
  0 correct transformations
  1 incorrect transformations
  0 failed-to-prove transformations
  0 Alive2 errors

